=========================================================================================================
16_leakage_ladder.py — How much of the published R2 = 0.85 comes from information leaks (TensorFlow environment)
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  The final model of the original study reached R2 = 0.85 on its test molecules. In its code,
  those test molecules also         decided which descriptors were kept and when training stopped,
  and part of them had been used to fit the data         preprocessing. Each of these lets the
  model see information about the molecules it is scored on, which makes the         score
  optimistic. This step removes the leaks one at a time (R0 = as published ... R4 = no leak left,
  duplicates         removed) and re-scores the model after each change, with the same split and
  the same random seeds. The drop between two         rungs is the part of the score that the
  removed leak was responsible for.
